/* Manu Tere · zh · pack marq · generated by build.py; loaded with the pack */
__mtLangPack('zh','marq',{"The Hakaui valley trail, between high cliffs, toward the Vaipo waterfall":"Hakaui 山谷的小径，穿行在高高的悬崖之间，通往 Vaipo 瀑布","A boat drops you in Hakatea bay. The trail climbs the Hakaui valley, past old stone platforms, to Vaipo, a waterfall about {#1} m high. Hold <b>Walk</b>.":"一艘小船把你送到 Hakatea 湾。小径沿 Hakaui 山谷向上，经过古老的石砌平台，通往高约 {#1} m 的 Vaipo 瀑布。按住<b>行走</b>。","A river crossing! Jump from stone to stone when the green zone is under your feet.":"要过河了！当绿色区域在你脚下时，从一块石头跳到另一块石头上。","One stone… and another!":"一块石头……再一块！","Splash! Wet feet. Try again: wait for the green zone.":"扑通！脚湿了。再试一次：等绿色区域出现。","Old paepae, stone house platforms, line the trail under the trees. The view would be great from the top. What do you do?":"古老的 paepae（房屋的石砌平台）排列在林下小径两旁。从顶上看风景一定很棒。你会怎么做？","Stay on the path and look from there":"留在小路上，从那里看","Yes. Paepae are fragile and part of the valley’s heritage: never climb them.":"对。Paepae 很脆弱，是山谷遗产的一部分：千万不要爬上去。","Climb up for a photo":"爬上去拍张照","No: the stones are fragile and the sites are respected. Stay on the path.":"不行：这些石头很脆弱，这些遗址也受到尊重。请留在小路上。","Nonos! Tiny biting sandflies. Tap them away, and next time wear long sleeves and repellent.":"Nono 来了！会咬人的小沙蝇。点击把它们赶走，下次记得穿长袖、涂驱虫剂。","Gone! On to the waterfall.":"赶走了！继续去瀑布吧。","Vaipo! The water falls from the top of the cliff into a deep pool.":"Vaipo 到了！水从悬崖顶上落进一个深潭。","Pacific rosewood (miro)":"太平洋桐棉（miro）","Dark reddish-brown heartwood, medium-hard. It was planted at sacred places, and carved into tiki and bowls.":"心材呈深红褐色，硬度中等。过去人们把它种在神圣之地，用来雕刻 tiki 和木碗。","Cordia (tou)":"破布木（tou）","Soft, easy to carve and resists termites. It does not flavour food, so it is good for bowls.":"木质软，易雕刻，还能防白蚁。它不会给食物带来异味，所以很适合做碗。","Ironwood (toa, ʻaito)":"铁木（toa，ʻaito）","Very hard and heavy: the wood of war clubs. A tough first tiki!":"非常坚硬沉重：是做战棍的木头。第一个 tiki 用它可不容易！","A reddish wood carved for many objects, from a tree once planted on sacred sites.":"一种微红的木头，可雕刻许多物件，这种树过去种在神圣之地。","A carver’s workshop in Taiohae, with a block of wood":"Taiohae 的一间木雕工坊，有一块木料","In Taiohae, a <b>tuhuna</b>, a master carver, lets you carve a small tiki. First choose the wood. Carvers dry it for years before carving.":"在 Taiohae，一位 <b>tuhuna</b>（木雕大师）让你雕一个小 tiki。先选木头。木雕师会把木头晾上好几年才开始雕刻。","<b>{#1}. Rough out the shape with the adze.</b> Long ago the adze blade was basalt. Tap each mark to cut away a chip.":"<b>{#1}. 用锛子凿出大致形状。</b>很久以前，锛子的刀刃是玄武岩做的。点击每个标记，削掉一块木屑。","<b>{#1}. Carve the face with the gouge.</b> Big round eyes, a wide mouth, hands on the belly: the tiki is the first man, the ancestor. Tap the dots in order.":"<b>{#1}. 用圆凿雕出面孔。</b>又大又圆的眼睛、宽宽的嘴、双手放在肚子上：tiki 是第一个人，是祖先。按顺序点击这些圆点。","<b>{#1}. Polish.</b> Rub with sand, then with ray skin, the old sandpaper of the islands, until the wood glows.":"<b>{#1}. 打磨。</b>先用沙子擦，再用鳐鱼皮擦（海岛上古老的砂纸），直到木头发亮。","Rub with sand":"用沙子擦","Rub with ray skin":"用鳐鱼皮擦","Your {A} tiki is finished, carved with a tuhuna of Taiohae. The carver keeps it to dry slowly; the real ones take years.":"你的{A} tiki 完成了，是和 Taiohae 的一位 tuhuna 一起雕的。木雕师会把它留下慢慢晾干；真正的 tiki 要晾好几年。","Designing a Marquesan tattoo band for your manu":"为你的 manu 设计一条马克萨斯文身纹带","In the Marquesas, <b>patutiki</b>, tattoo, told who you were: your family, your strength, your protection. Motifs are personal, so you will design your own band, never copy someone else’s. Choose <b>{#1} motifs</b>.":"在马克萨斯群岛，<b>patutiki</b>（文身）诉说你是谁：你的家族、你的力量、你的守护。图案是个人的，所以你要设计属于自己的纹带，绝不照抄别人的。选择 <b>{#1} 个图案</b>。","Give the design to the tuhuna":"把设计交给 tuhuna","Three motifs for one band. Tap one to remove it.":"一条纹带三个图案。点击一个可以移除。","The <b>tuhuna patutiki</b> works with a comb of bone and a little mallet, and an ink of candlenut soot. Today’s masters use modern machines, with the same motifs. Tap in rhythm.":"<b>tuhuna patutiki</b> 用骨制的梳状针和一把小木槌工作，墨水用石栗烧出的烟灰制成。如今的大师使用现代文身机，图案却还是一样。跟着节奏点击。","Tap · tap":"点 · 点","<b>Aftercare.</b> Long ago a fresh tattoo was covered with tapa and soothed with noni leaves and scented oil.":"<b>护理。</b>很久以前，新文身会用 tapa 盖住，再用 noni 叶和香油舒缓。","Lay a noni leaf":"敷上一片 noni 叶","Your manu wears its own patutiki band: {A}. Remember: ask before photographing a tattooed person, and never copy someone’s motifs.":"你的 manu 戴上了属于自己的 patutiki 纹带：{A}。记住：给有文身的人拍照前先征得同意，也绝不照抄别人的图案。","Wet pebbles at the water’s edge on Hohoi beach":"Hohoi 海滩水边湿漉漉的卵石","On Hohoi beach, some pebbles are <b>flower stones</b>: volcanic rock with pale “petals” of crystals inside. When they are dry the flowers hide. Wait for a wave, then tap the stones that show a flower. Find {#1}.":"在 Hohoi 海滩，有些卵石是<b>花石</b>：火山岩里藏着淡色晶体组成的“花瓣”。石头干的时候，花就藏起来了。等一个浪打过来，再点击露出花纹的石头。找到 {#1} 块。","Dry stones hide their flowers. Wait for the next wave.":"干石头会把花藏起来。等下一个浪吧。","A flower stone! It even rings when you tap it.":"一块花石！点一下它还会叮当作响。","Just basalt, no flowers in this one.":"只是玄武岩，这块没有花。","At the craft centre in Hakahau, carvers turn flower stones into pendants. Follow the steps.":"在 Hakahau 的手工艺中心，雕刻师把花石做成吊坠。跟着步骤来。","Rough-cut with the grinder":"用砂轮机粗切","Sketch the shape and cut":"画出形状并切割","Sand, finer and finer":"打磨，越磨越细","Polish until the flower shines":"抛光，直到花纹发亮","You found three flower stones on Hohoi beach and polished one into a pendant. This stone is found in very few places in the world.":"你在 Hohoi 海滩找到了三块花石，并把其中一块磨成了吊坠。世界上只有极少数地方能找到这种石头。","Open the wings":"展开翅膀","A dance place under the needles of Ua Pou, with a pahu drum":"Ua Pou 石峰下的舞场，有一面 pahu 鼓","In Marquesan dances, the dancers sometimes become birds, arms spread like wings. Watch the dancer on the left, then repeat the moves in the same order, on the beat of the <b>pahu</b>.":"在马克萨斯舞蹈中，舞者有时会化身为鸟，双臂像翅膀一样张开。看左边的舞者，然后跟着 <b>pahu</b> 的鼓点，按同样的顺序重复动作。","Watch…":"看好……","Your turn!":"轮到你了！","Not quite: move {A} was “{B}”. Watch again.":"差一点：第 {A} 个动作是“{B}”。再看一遍。","Beautiful!":"真漂亮！","About {#1} m tall: the tallest tiki in French Polynesia. Your manu would reach its knees!":"高约 {#1} m：法属波利尼西亚最高的 tiki。你的 manu 只够到它的膝盖！","The only known tiki carved lying down, on its belly, arms stretched forward.":"已知唯一一尊趴着雕刻的 tiki，肚子朝下，双臂向前伸。","A smaller tiki":"一尊较小的 tiki","Several smaller tiki stand on the terraces of the meʻae.":"meʻae 的石台上立着好几尊较小的 tiki。","A carved head":"一个雕刻的头像","Some tiki have been worn by centuries of rain: look closely for the eyes and mouth.":"有些 tiki 已被几百年的雨水磨蚀：仔细找找眼睛和嘴巴。","The meʻae Iipona at Puamau, stone terraces with tiki among the trees":"Puamau 的 meʻae Iipona，林间的石台上立着 tiki","The meʻae Iipona, in the valley of Puamau, is the largest historic site of the Marquesas. Your guide asks you to find <b>{#1} tiki</b> among the stone terraces. Tap them.":"meʻae Iipona 位于 Puamau 山谷，是马克萨斯群岛最大的历史遗址。你的向导请你在石台间找出 <b>{#1} 尊 tiki</b>。点击它们。","Your guide reminds you of the rules of the meʻae. Which one is right?":"你的向导提醒你 meʻae 的规矩。哪一条是对的？","Stay off the stones, keep quiet, take nothing away":"不踩石头，保持安静，什么都不带走","Yes. A meʻae is a sacred place: walk around, listen to your guide.":"对。meʻae 是神圣之地：绕着走，听向导讲解。","Sit on a tiki’s shoulders for a photo":"坐在 tiki 的肩膀上拍张照","Never: tiki are sacred, and very old. Photograph them from the ground.":"绝对不行：tiki 是神圣的，而且非常古老。请站在地面上拍照。","Picnic on the top terrace":"在最高的石台上野餐","No picnics or fires on sacred sites. There is a place for that in the village.":"神圣遗址上不能野餐或生火。村子里有专门的地方。","You found Takaiʻi and the other tiki of the meʻae Iipona, and kept the rules of a sacred place.":"你找到了 Takaiʻi 和 meʻae Iipona 的其他 tiki，也遵守了神圣之地的规矩。","Roasting a breadfruit on a wood fire, then pounding it in a wooden bowl":"在柴火上烤面包果，然后在木碗里捣碎","<b>{#1}. Roast the mei.</b> Put the breadfruit right on the fire and turn it until the skin is black all over.":"<b>{#1}. 烤 mei。</b>把面包果直接放在火上，不停翻动，直到外皮全部烤黑。","Turn the breadfruit":"翻动面包果","Wait until this side is black.":"等这一面烤黑。","<b>{#1}. Peel.</b> Let it cool a little, then scrape off the black skin.":"<b>{#1}. 去皮。</b>让它稍微凉一凉，再刮掉烤黑的外皮。","<b>{#1}. Pound.</b> Into the <b>umete</b>, the carved wooden bowl, and pound with the <b>penu</b>, the stone pestle, until it is smooth.":"<b>{#1}. 捣。</b>放进 <b>umete</b>（雕刻的木碗），用 <b>penu</b>（石杵）捣，直到变得细滑。","Pound!":"捣！","<b>{#1}. Coconut milk.</b> Pour fresh coconut milk over the smooth kaʻaku.":"<b>{#1}. 椰奶。</b>把新鲜椰奶浇在细滑的 kaʻaku 上。","Pour the coconut milk":"浇上椰奶","Your kaʻaku is ready. You can now cook it in your own faʻaʻapu kitchen too, with an ʻuru and a coconut.":"你的 kaʻaku 做好了。现在你也可以在自己的 faʻaʻapu 厨房里，用一个 ʻuru 和一个椰子来做它。","Paper mulberry":"构树","Gives the whitest, finest tapa.":"做出最白、最细的 tapa。","Banyan":"榕树","Gives a warm brown tapa.":"做出暖褐色的 tapa。","Breadfruit (mei)":"面包果树（mei）","Gives a light brown tapa.":"做出浅褐色的 tapa。","Making tapa on Fatu Hiva":"在 Fatu Hiva 制作 tapa","On Fatu Hiva, women make <b>tapa</b>, bark cloth, as their mothers taught them. First choose the bark.":"在 Fatu Hiva，女人们按照母亲传授的方法制作 <b>tapa</b>（树皮布）。先选树皮。","{#1}. Scrape, slit and peel.":"{#1}. 刮皮、划开、剥皮。","Scrape off the outer skin, slit the branch along its length, and peel away the inner bark with a wooden spatula.":"刮掉外皮，沿枝条纵向划开，再用木铲剥下内层树皮。","Scrape · slit · peel":"刮 · 划 · 剥","<b>{#1}. Soak</b> the strip of inner bark in water to soften it.":"<b>{#1}. 浸泡</b>内层树皮条，让它在水里变软。","{#1}. Beat it":"{#1}. 捶打它","on a wooden anvil with a grooved beater: first the coarse grooves, then the fine ones. The bark spreads to four or five times its width.":"在木砧上用带槽的捶棒捶：先用粗槽，再用细槽。树皮会展宽到原来的四五倍。","Beat!":"捶！","<b>{#1}. Dry it in the shade,</b> stretched flat, with a stone on each corner.":"<b>{#1}. 在阴凉处晾干，</b>摊平，每个角压一块石头。","<b>{#1}. Decorate</b> with brown and black plant dyes. Choose up to {#2} motifs, like those of tattoo.":"<b>{#1}. 装饰</b>，用褐色和黑色的植物染料。最多选 {#2} 个图案，就像文身图案那样。","Add at least one motif.":"至少加一个图案。","The woven base of the bouquet.":"花束的编织底座。","Ylang-ylang":"依兰","Long yellow petals, a heady scent.":"长长的黄色花瓣，香气浓郁。","The white gardenia of the islands.":"海岛上的白色栀子花。","Plumeria, white and yellow.":"缅栀花，白色和黄色。","Tiny white stars.":"小小的白色星星。","Miri (basil)":"Miri（罗勒）","A fresh, green scent.":"清新的绿叶香。","Pineapple pieces":"菠萝块","Rolled in sandalwood powder.":"裹上檀香粉。","Sandalwood powder":"檀香粉","Puahi: rare and precious.":"Puahi：稀有而珍贵。","An umu hei, a scented bouquet, being made in Omoa":"在 Omoa 制作一束 umu hei 香花束","In Omoa, a family shows you how to make an <b>umu hei</b>, a scented bouquet worn in the hair. Add the plants in the right order: the pandanus base first, then <b>three flowers</b>, then green miri, and last the pineapple rolled in sandalwood.":"在 Omoa，一户人家教你制作 <b>umu hei</b>，一种戴在头发上的香花束。按正确的顺序加入植物：先放露兜树叶底座，再放<b>三种花</b>，然后是绿色的 miri，最后是裹了檀香粉的菠萝。","Start with the pandanus: it holds everything.":"先放露兜树叶：它能托住所有东西。","Three flowers first.":"先放三种花。","Now the green miri.":"现在放绿色的 miri。","Last: pineapple and sandalwood.":"最后：菠萝和檀香。","You danced like a bird under the needles of Ua Pou, without a single mistake. Ua Pou hosted the first Matavaʻa, the Marquesas arts festival, in {#1}.":"你在 Ua Pou 的尖峰下像鸟一样跳舞，一次都没出错。{#1} 年，Ua Pou 举办了第一届马克萨斯艺术节 Matavaʻa。","<span>Kaikai meitai!</span> Your kaʻaku is ready. You can now cook it in your own faʻaʻapu kitchen too, with an ʻuru and a coconut.":"<span>Kaikai meitai!</span> 你的 kaʻaku 做好了。现在你也可以在自己的 faʻaʻapu 厨房里用一个 ʻuru 和一个椰子来做它。","<b>{#1}. Scrape, slit and peel.</b> Scrape off the outer skin, slit the branch along its length, and peel away the inner bark with a wooden spatula.":"<b>{#1}. 刮皮、剖开、剥下。</b>刮掉外层表皮，把树枝纵向剖开，再用木铲剥下内层树皮。","<b>{#1}. Beat it</b> on a wooden anvil with a grooved beater: first the coarse grooves, then the fine ones. The bark spreads to four or five times its width.":"<b>{#1}. 捶打它</b>，放在木砧上用带凹槽的捶棒捶打：先用粗槽，再用细槽。树皮会被捶展到原来宽度的四五倍。","Your umu hei is ready. People say its scent makes the wearer irresistible. Sandalwood is endangered today: it is being replanted on Nuku Hiva and Hiva Oa.":"你的 umu hei 做好了。据说它的香气能让佩戴者魅力无法抗拒。如今檀香木已濒危：人们正在 Nuku Hiva 和 Hiva Oa 重新种植。","You reached Vaipo, the great waterfall of the Hakaui valley, after {#1} splashes in the river.":"你到达了 Hakaui 山谷的大瀑布 Vaipo，途中在河里溅了 {#1} 次水。","You reached Vaipo, the great waterfall of the Hakaui valley, with dry feet.":"你到达了 Hakaui 山谷的大瀑布 Vaipo，双脚一点没湿。","You danced like a bird under the needles of Ua Pou, after {#1} tries. Ua Pou hosted the first Matavaʻa, the Marquesas arts festival, in {#2}.":"你在 Ua Pou 的尖峰下像鸟一样跳舞，试了 {#1} 次。{#2} 年，Ua Pou 举办了第一届马克萨斯艺术节 Matavaʻa。","Your umu hei is ready, made in the right order the first time. People say its scent makes the wearer irresistible. Sandalwood is endangered today: it is being replanted on Nuku Hiva and Hiva Oa.":"你的 umu hei 做好了，第一次就按正确的顺序完成。据说它的香气能让佩戴者魅力无法抗拒。如今檀香木已濒危：人们正在 Nuku Hiva 和 Hiva Oa 重新种植。","Your tapa ({A}) is beaten, dried and painted with your own motifs. On Fatu Hiva the bark is cut when the moon is right, when “the flesh of the tree is full”.":"你的 tapa（{A}）已经捶好、晾干，并画上了你自己的图案。在 Fatu Hiva，要等月相合适、“树的肉饱满”时才割树皮。","You have no {A} left: {B}":"你已经没有 {A} 了：{B}","You reached Vaipo, the great waterfall of the Hakaui valley, after {A} splashes in the river.":"你在河里扑腾了 {A} 次之后，终于到达了 Hakaui 山谷的大瀑布 Vaipo。","You danced like a bird under the needles of Ua Pou, after {A} tries. Ua Pou hosted the first Matavaʻa, the Marquesas arts festival, in 1987.":"你尝试了 {A} 次，终于在 Ua Pou 的尖峰下像鸟儿一样跳起了舞。1987 年，Ua Pou 举办了第一届马克萨斯艺术节 Matavaʻa。","The craft stall in Taiohae":"Taiohae 的手工艺摊","A visitor greets you: <span>Kaʻoha!</span> and asks for":"一位游客跟你打招呼：<span>Kaʻoha!</span>，然后想要","Customers served":"已服务顾客","Marquesan counts its own way. Put the {A} on the mat, then wrap them.":"马克萨斯语有自己的数数方式。把 {A} 放到草席上，然后包起来。","A carving":"一件雕刻","On the mat: <b>{B}</b>":"草席上：<b>{B}</b>","Wrap them":"包起来","is {B}. In Tahitian you would say":"就是 {B}。在塔希提语里，你会说","Five customers served. They leave saying":"五位顾客都服务好了。他们离开时说","Count again: the visitor asked for {A}.":"再数一遍：游客要的是 {A}。","Flutter the feathers":"抖动羽毛","Dip low":"压低身体","Dusk on a stone platform under the needles of Ua Pou: a drummer, three dancers and your manu, all wearing white feather crowns":"黄昏时分，Ua Pou 的尖峰下的一座石台上：一位鼓手、三位舞者和你的 manu，都戴着白色羽毛冠","In the Marquesan bird dance, <b>haka manu</b>, the dancers become birds. Listen to the <b>pahu</b>: the lead dances one move on each beat. Then <b>repeat the moves in the same order</b>, on the beat if you can.":"在马克萨斯的鸟舞 <b>haka manu</b> 中，舞者化身为鸟。听着 <b>pahu</b> 鼓声：领舞者每一拍跳一个动作。然后<b>按同样的顺序重复这些动作</b>，尽量踩在拍子上。","Right move, a little off the beat.":"动作对了，稍微偏离了拍子。","Beautiful! The crowd claps.":"太美了！观众在鼓掌。",", after one more look":"，又多看了一遍之后",", after {A} more looks":"，又多看了 {A} 遍之后","You danced like a bird under the needles of Ua Pou{A}, with {B} moves on the beat of the pahu. Ua Pou hosted the first Matavaʻa, the Marquesas arts festival, in 1987.":"你在 Ua Pou 的尖峰下像鸟一样起舞{A}，有 {B} 个动作踩在了 pahu 的鼓点上。Ua Pou 在 1987 年举办了第一届马克萨斯艺术节 Matavaʻa。","The emblem of the meʻae, on the rear platform. Carved in red volcanic tuff,":"这座 meʻae 的象征，位于后方的石台上。由红色火山凝灰岩雕成的",", it stands {#1} m above the ground: the largest tiki in French Polynesia. Look at its massive square head, and its left arm, partly broken.":"，高出地面 {#1} 米：是法属波利尼西亚最大的 tiki。看看它巨大的方形头部，还有部分断裂的左臂。","Further back, also in red tuff and about {#1} m tall. It sits with its legs straight and spread, the way women sat to work on the ground. It is thought to be Takaiʻi’s wife.":"在更后面，同样是红色凝灰岩，高约 {#1} 米。它双腿伸直分开坐着，就像过去女人坐在地上干活的样子。人们认为它是 Takaiʻi 的妻子。","In grey tuff, slimmer and better balanced. Its hands are clearly carved. Its head had broken off: archaeologists set it back in place.":"由灰色凝灰岩雕成，更修长，比例更匀称。它的双手雕得很清楚。它的头曾经断落：考古学家把它安放回了原位。","On the first platform, in pale grey tuff: a woman lying face down, head thrown back and eyes turned to the sky, mouth open with the tongue showing. Specialists think she is giving birth. The animals carved on her pedestal look like dogs: their meaning is unknown.":"在第一座石台上，由浅灰色凝灰岩雕成：一个女人脸朝下趴着，头向后仰，眼睛望向天空，张着嘴，露出舌头。专家认为她正在分娩。她底座上雕刻的动物看起来像狗：含义不明。","On a lower platform to the left: roughly worked, without a head, and hard to read. Count the fingers: six on each hand.":"在左边一座较低的石台上：雕得很粗糙，没有头，很难辨认。数数它的手指：每只手有六根。","The meʻae Iipona at Puamau: stone terraces under banyans and breadfruit trees, with five great tiki":"Puamau 的 meʻae Iipona：榕树和面包树下的石砌台地，有五尊大 tiki","The meʻae Iipona, in the valley of Puamau, is the largest historic site of the Marquesas. Your guide asks you to find its <b>{#1} great tiki</b> among the stone terraces. Tap them.":"位于 Puamau 山谷的 meʻae Iipona 是马克萨斯群岛最大的历史遗址。你的向导请你在石砌台地间找出它的 <b>{#1} 尊大 tiki</b>。点击它们。","You found Takaiʻi, Fau Poe, Manuiotaʻa, Makiʻi Taua Pepe and Te Tovae E Noho, the five great tiki of the meʻae Iipona, and kept the rules of a sacred place.":"你找到了 Takaiʻi、Fau Poe、Manuiotaʻa、Makiʻi Taua Pepe 和 Te Tovae E Noho——meʻae Iipona 的五尊大 tiki，并且遵守了圣地的规矩。","The Hakaui valley trail, between sheer basalt walls, toward the Vaipo waterfall":"Hakaui 山谷步道，穿行在陡峭的玄武岩崖壁之间，通往 Vaipo 瀑布","A boat drops you in Hakatea bay. The trail climbs the Hakaui valley, between walls of basalt, past old stone platforms, to Vaipo, a waterfall about {#1} m high. Hold <b>Walk</b>.":"一条船把你送到 Hakatea 湾。步道沿着 Hakaui 山谷向上，穿过玄武岩崖壁之间，经过古老的石台，通往高约 {#1} 米的 Vaipo 瀑布。按住<b>行走</b>。","A river crossing! Jump from stone to stone when the marker is in the green zone.":"要过河了！当标记在绿色区域时，从一块石头跳到另一块石头上。","Splash! Wet feet. Wait for the green zone.":"扑通！脚湿了。等到绿色区域再跳。","Nono! Tiny biting sandflies buzz around your manu. Tap them away.":"Nono！会叮人的小沙蝇在你的 manu 周围嗡嗡乱飞。点击把它们赶走。","A nono":"一只 nono（一种会叮人的小沙蝇）","Gone… for now.":"赶走了……暂时。","Nono bite near rivers and beaches, mostly in the morning and late afternoon. How do walkers avoid them?":"nono（一种会叮人的小沙蝇）常在河边和海滩叮人，大多在早上和傍晚。徒步的人怎样避开它们？","Long sleeves, long trousers and repellent":"长袖、长裤和驱虫剂","Yes. Their bites itch for days: cover up and use repellent before the walk.":"对。被它们叮了会痒好几天：出发前穿好衣服遮住皮肤，涂上驱虫剂。","Scratch the bites so they heal faster":"抓挠叮咬处，好得更快","No: scratching can infect the bites. Cover up and use repellent instead.":"不对：抓挠可能让叮咬处感染。还是穿好衣服遮住皮肤，涂上驱虫剂吧。","On to the waterfall.":"继续前往瀑布。","The cargo ship cannot come alongside the little pier of Vaipaeʻe, so a boat brings the goods ashore. Ua Huka has <b>no black rats</b>, and that is why the pihiti still lives here. A single rat hidden in the cargo could change everything.":"货轮无法停靠 Vaipaeʻe 的小码头，所以由小船把货物运上岸。Ua Huka <b>没有黑家鼠</b>，正因如此，pihiti 至今还生活在这里。货物里只要藏着一只老鼠，就可能改变一切。","Meet <b>Tip</b>, a rat-detector dog of the island's bird association, and her handler. <b>Tap each load</b> to send Tip to sniff it. If she smells a rat, she sits and stares.":"来认识一下 <b>Tip</b>：它是岛上鸟类协会的嗅鼠犬，旁边是它的训犬员。<b>点击每一批货物</b>，让 Tip 去嗅一嗅。如果它闻到老鼠，就会坐下来盯着看。","Reward Tip":"奖励 Tip","Seal the load and set traps":"封好货物，布下捕鼠器","Tip gets her toy and a pat.":"Tip 得到了它的玩具，还被摸了摸头。","The team wraps the load in a sealed sheet and sets traps all round it. In the morning, a <b>black rat</b> is in a trap. It never touched the island.":"团队用密封布把货物包起来，并在四周布下捕鼠器。第二天早上，一只<b>黑家鼠</b>落进了捕鼠器。它从没碰到这座岛。","Now <b>check the five trap stations</b> along the wharf, as the team does every month.":"现在<b>检查码头边的五个捕鼠站</b>，就像团队每个月做的那样。","Station {#1} of {#2}: empty.":"第 {#1} 个捕鼠站（共 {#2} 个）：空的。","All five stations are empty: no black rat on the wharf.":"五个捕鼠站都是空的：码头上没有黑家鼠。","The small wharf of Vaipaeʻe: a boat has brought the cargo ashore, and a detector dog checks it":"Vaipaeʻe 的小码头：一艘小船把货物运上了岸，一只嗅鼠犬正在检查","You join the bird society's count in a valley of Ua Huka. You stand still at one point for a few minutes and count every bird you see. <b>Tap each bird once</b> when it lands: the pihiti in the coconut and pūrau flowers, the black patiʻotiʻo in the leaves, and the big upe, a pigeon brought here from Nuku Hiva to keep it safe.":"你加入鸟类协会，在 Ua Huka 的一条山谷里数鸟。你在一个点上静静站几分钟，数下看到的每一只鸟。鸟落下时，<b>每只鸟点击一次</b>：椰子花和 pūrau 花间的 pihiti，树叶里黑色的 patiʻotiʻo，还有大个子的 upe，一种为了保护它而从 Nuku Hiva 引来这里的鸽子。","Already counted: count each bird once.":"已经数过了：每只鸟只数一次。","Time. Your count: <b>{#1} pihiti, {#2} patiʻotiʻo, {#3} upe</b>. There were {#4}, {#5} and {#6}: you counted <b>{#7}%</b> of the birds.":"时间到。你的计数：<b>{#1} 只 pihiti、{#2} 只 patiʻotiʻo、{#3} 只 upe</b>。实际有 {#4}、{#5} 和 {#6} 只：你数到了 <b>{#7}%</b> 的鸟。","Counts like this, repeated at many points every few years, tell the society whether the birds are doing well.":"像这样每隔几年在许多地点重复计数，协会就能知道鸟儿们过得好不好。","A forest valley of Ua Huka with coconut palms and pūrau trees in flower":"Ua Huka 的一条森林山谷，椰子树和 pūrau 树正在开花","You counted the birds of a valley of Ua Huka with the bird society: {#1}% of the birds that came by. About {#2} pihiti live on the island today, the last of their kind, and the patiʻotiʻo is found nowhere else. Counting them again and again is how we know they are safe.":"你和鸟类协会一起数了 Ua Huka 一条山谷里的鸟：数到了飞过的鸟中的 {#1}%。如今岛上生活着约 {#2} 只 pihiti，是这个物种最后的一群；patiʻotiʻo 也是别处都没有的。一次又一次地数它们，我们才知道它们是安全的。","The dancers of Ua Huka brought back the <span>haka manu</span>, the bird dance, with feathers. First weave the base of your costume: a cape of coconut fibre. <b>Tap Weave</b> six times.":"Ua Huka 的舞者让 <span>haka manu</span>，也就是插着羽毛的鸟舞，重新跳了起来。先编织服饰的底子：一件椰纤披肩。<b>点击“编织”</b>六次。","Only feathers found on the ground: a living bird is never plucked.":"只用在地上捡到的羽毛：绝不从活鸟身上拔毛。","Row {#1} of {#2}. <b>Choose what to tie on</b>: one of the feathers you picked up on the islands, or a fringe of fibre if you have no feather to spare.":"第 {#1} 排（共 {#2} 排）。<b>选择要系上的东西</b>：你在各岛捡到的一根羽毛，或者在没有多余羽毛时，系一束纤维流苏。","No crest":"不戴羽冠","Now dance the <span>haka manu</span> with the troupe. The leader calls each move: <b>wings up</b> like a bird taking off, or <b>wings down</b> like a bird landing. Follow six calls.":"现在和舞团一起跳 <span>haka manu</span>。领舞者喊出每个动作：<b>展翅</b>，像鸟儿起飞；或者<b>收翅</b>，像鸟儿落地。跟上六次口令。","Wings up":"展翅","Wings down":"收翅","Wings down!":"收翅！","Wings up!":"展翅！","a crate of tinned food":"一箱罐头食品","You made a costume for the bird dance: a cape of coconut fibre with four rows ({A}){B}, and danced the haka manu with the troupe, {C} of 6 moves in time. Your manu can wear it: every feather in it was found on the ground.":"你做了一套鸟舞服饰：一件有四排装饰的椰纤披肩（{A}）{B}，还和舞团一起跳了 haka manu，6 个动作中有 {C} 个合拍。你的 manu 可以穿上它：上面的每一根羽毛都是在地上捡到的。","a box of outboard parts":"一箱舷外机零件","cartons of drinks":"几箱饮料","sacks of rice":"几袋大米","one load":"一批货物","Choose a feather, or go without.":"选一根羽毛，或者不戴。","sacks of flour":"几袋面粉","You counted the birds of a valley of Ua Huka with the bird society: {A}% of the birds that came by. About 1,800 pihiti live on the island today, the last of their kind, and the patiʻotiʻo is found nowhere else. Counting them again and again is how we know they are safe.":"你和鸟类协会一起数了 Ua Huka 一条山谷里的鸟：数到了飞过的鸟中的 {A}%。如今岛上生活着约 1,800 只 pihiti，是这个物种最后的一群；patiʻotiʻo 也是别处都没有的。一次又一次地数它们，我们才知道它们是安全的。","bags of cement":"几袋水泥","You have no feather left: the crest can wait.":"你已经没有羽毛了：羽冠可以以后再说。","<b>Tip sits and stares at {A}.</b> That is her sign: a rat is hiding there. First, reward her: a good dog is paid in play.":"<b>Tip 坐下来，盯着{A}。</b>这是它的信号：那里藏着一只老鼠。先奖励它：对好狗狗的报酬就是陪它玩。","The other way: watch the leader.":"做反了：看领舞者。","Your manu and the costume taking shape":"你的 manu 和渐渐成形的服饰","a crate of plates":"一箱盘子","a roll of fencing":"一卷围栏网","Tip has already checked that one.":"Tip 已经检查过那一批了。","Last, the crest on the head. {A}":"最后是头上的羽冠。{A}","Station {A} of 5: empty.":"第 {A} 个捕鼠站（共 5 个）：空的。","Tip checked {A} and found the rat hidden in {B}. The load was sealed and the rat trapped before it reached the island, and the trap stations on the wharf stayed empty. On Ua Huka this check is done at every cargo ship, with dogs trained in New Zealand.":"Tip 检查了{A}，发现老鼠藏在{B}里。货物被封好，老鼠在登岛前就被捕获，码头上的捕鼠站也一直是空的。在 Ua Huka，每艘货轮到港都要做这样的检查，用的是在新西兰训练的狗。","Tip sniffs {A}, wags and moves on: nothing there.":"Tip 嗅了嗅{A}，摇摇尾巴走开了：那里什么也没有。","Time. Your count: <b>{A} pihiti, {B} patiʻotiʻo, {C} upe</b>. There were {D}, {E} and {F}: you counted <b>{G}%</b> of the birds.":"时间到。你的计数：<b>{A} 只 pihiti、{B} 只 patiʻotiʻo、{C} 只 upe</b>。实际有 {D}、{E} 和 {F} 只：你数到了 <b>{G}%</b> 的鸟。","Row {A} of 4. <b>Choose what to tie on</b>: one of the feathers you picked up on the islands, or a fringe of fibre if you have no feather to spare.":"第 {A} 排（共 4 排）。<b>选择要系上的东西</b>：你在各岛捡到的一根羽毛，或者在没有多余羽毛时，系一束纤维流苏。","The narrow bay of Vaipaeʻe between dark cliffs, the cargo ship turning inside it, a barge at the small quay, and a detector dog checking the loads":"深色悬崖之间狭窄的 Vaipaeʻe 海湾，货轮正在湾内掉头，一艘驳船停在小码头边，一只嗅鼠犬正在检查货物","Vaipaeʻe, the “invisible bay”: a long cleft between dark cliffs, its mouth only {#1} m wide. The cargo ship turns right round inside it, and a barge brings the loads to the small quay. Ua Huka has <b>no black rats</b>, and that is why the pihiti still lives here: a single rat hidden in a load could change everything.":"Vaipaeʻe，“看不见的海湾”：深色悬崖之间一道长长的裂口，湾口只有 {#1} 米宽。货轮在湾内整个掉过头来，再由驳船把货物运到小码头。Ua Huka <b>没有黑家鼠</b>，正因如此，pihiti 至今还生活在这里：货物里只要藏着一只老鼠，就可能改变一切。","Meet <b>Tip</b>, a rat-detector dog of the island’s bird association, and her handler. <b>Tap each load</b> to send Tip to sniff it. If she smells a rat, she sits and stares.":"来认识一下 <b>Tip</b>：它是岛上鸟类协会的嗅鼠犬，旁边是它的训犬员。<b>点击每一批货物</b>，让 Tip 去嗅一嗅。如果它闻到老鼠，就会坐下来盯着看。","Throw the ball":"扔球","Tip brings the ball back, tail going. Good dog.":"Tip 把球叼了回来，尾巴摇个不停。好狗狗。","Seal the load":"封好货物","The team wraps the load in a sealed sheet so nothing can get out. Now <b>set four traps</b> round it: tap the four marks.":"团队用密封布把货物包起来，让什么都跑不出来。现在在它四周<b>布下四个捕鼠器</b>：点击四个标记。","Trap {#1} of {#2} set, baited with peanut butter.":"第 {#1} 个捕鼠器（共 {#2} 个）已布好，用花生酱做诱饵。","Wait for the morning":"等到早上","<b>Morning.</b> The sun comes over the cliff. <b>Open the four traps</b> one by one.":"<b>早上。</b>太阳从悬崖上升起。<b>逐个打开四个捕鼠器</b>。","<b>A black rat</b>, in the trap. It never touched the island.":"<b>一只黑家鼠</b>，在捕鼠器里。它从没碰到这座岛。","One more job, done every month: the <b>tracking tunnels</b> along the quay. A tunnel with bait and an ink pad: whatever walks through leaves its footprints on a card. <b>Tap the five tunnels</b> in turn and read the cards.":"还有一项每个月都要做的工作：码头边的<b>足迹隧道</b>。隧道里放着诱饵和一块墨垫：无论什么走过去，都会把脚印留在卡片上。<b>依次点击五条隧道</b>，读一读卡片。","A clean card: nothing walked through this tunnel.":"一张干净的卡片：没有东西走过这条隧道。","Tiny claw marks on the ink card: a <b>land crab</b> walked through at night. Not a rat.":"墨卡上有细小的爪痕：一只<b>陆蟹</b>夜里走过。不是老鼠。","Little starry feet: a <b>gecko</b>. Not a rat.":"小小的星形脚印：一只<b>壁虎</b>。不是老鼠。","You join the bird society’s count in the green valley above Vaipaeʻe, where the stream comes down between the coconut palms and the pūrau in flower. You stand still at one point and <b>count every bird that lands</b> in sixty seconds. <b>Tap a bird</b> to look at it through the binoculars, then <b>name it</b>: the pihiti, the patiʻotiʻo, the upe brought here from Nuku Hiva, or another bird.":"你加入鸟类协会的计数，来到 Vaipaeʻe 上方的绿色山谷，溪水从椰子树和开花的 pūrau 之间流下来。你在一个点上静静站着，在六十秒内<b>数下落下的每一只鸟</b>。<b>点击一只鸟</b>，用望远镜看看它，然后<b>说出它的名字</b>：pihiti、patiʻotiʻo、从 Nuku Hiva 引来这里的 upe，或者别的鸟。","Tap a bird, then name it.":"点击一只鸟，然后说出它的名字。","<b>A myna</b>: brought from elsewhere, it is not in the count.":"<b>一只家八哥</b>：从外地引进来的，不算在计数里。","The society repeats counts like this at many points every few years: that is how we know the pihiti holds at about {#1} birds.":"协会每隔几年就在许多地点重复这样的计数：我们就是这样知道 pihiti 的数量稳定在约 {#1} 只。","A valley of Ua Huka: dry brown ridges above, coconut palms, a pūrau in flower and a breadfruit tree below, the counting point by the stream":"Ua Huka 的一条山谷：上方是干燥的褐色山脊，下方有椰子树、一棵开花的 pūrau 和一棵面包树，计数点就在溪边","You counted the birds of a valley of Ua Huka with the bird society: {#1}% of the birds that came by, each named through the binoculars. About {#2} pihiti live on the island today, the last of their kind, and the patiʻotiʻo is found nowhere else. Counting them again and again is how we know they are safe.":"你和鸟类协会一起数了 Ua Huka 一条山谷里的鸟：数到了飞过的鸟中的 {#1}%，每一只都是通过望远镜认出名字的。如今岛上生活着约 {#2} 只 pihiti，是这个物种最后的一群；patiʻotiʻo 也是别处都没有的。一次又一次地数它们，我们才知道它们是安全的。","The dancers of Ua Huka brought back the <span>haka manu</span>, the bird dance, with feathers. Regalia take months: the fibre is gathered, dried and twisted first. On the frame, <b>weave the cape</b> of coconut fibre over the warps: tap Weave six times.":"Ua Huka 的舞者让插着羽毛的 <span>haka manu</span>，也就是鸟舞，重新跳了起来。做一套盛装要花几个月：先要采集纤维，晒干，搓成线。在框架上，用椰子纤维在经线上<b>编织披肩</b>：点击“编织”六次。","Row {#1} of {#2}. <b>Choose what to tie on</b>, then tap Tie for each of the five feathers: a feather you picked up on the islands, or a fringe of dyed fibre if you have none to spare.":"第 {#1} 排（共 {#2} 排）。<b>选择要系上的东西</b>，然后点击“系上”，五根羽毛各一次：你在各岛捡到的一根羽毛，或者在没有多余羽毛时，一束染色的纤维流苏。","On the stone <span>tohua</span> the pahu start, and the troupe lines up behind you. The leader calls each move of the <span>haka manu</span>: <b>wings up</b> like a bird taking off, <b>wings down</b> like a bird landing, <b>turn</b> like a bird on a branch. Follow eight calls.":"在石砌的 <span>tohua</span> 上，pahu 敲响了，舞团在你身后排成队。领舞者喊出 <span>haka manu</span> 的每个动作：<b>展翅</b>，像鸟儿起飞；<b>收翅</b>，像鸟儿落地；<b>转身</b>，像枝头上的鸟儿。跟上八次口令。","The costume on its frame, then the dance on the stone tohua with the drummers and the troupe":"框架上的服饰，然后是在石砌 tohua 上与鼓手和舞团一起跳的舞","Like a bird.":"像鸟儿一样。","The troupe follows you.":"舞团跟着你。","Choose a feather for the crest, or go without.":"选一根羽毛做羽冠，或者不戴。","brown with a yellow mask: an introduced bird, not counted":"褐色，带黄色的眼罩：外来引入的鸟，不计数","<b>Tip sits and stares at {A}.</b> That is her sign: a rat is hiding in there. First, reward her: a good dog is paid in play.":"<b>Tip 坐下来，盯着{A}。</b>这是它的信号：那里藏着一只老鼠。先奖励它：对好狗狗的报酬就是陪它玩。","Last, the <b>headband</b>: a strip of tapa painted with the marks of the island, and a crest on top. {A}":"最后是<b>头带</b>：一条画着岛上图案的 tapa 布条，顶上再加一个羽冠。{A}","You made a costume for the bird dance: a cape of coconut fibre woven on the frame, four rows of feathers ({A}), a painted tapa headband{B}, and danced the haka manu on the tohua with the troupe, {C} of 8 calls in time. Your manu can wear it: every feather in it was found on the ground.":"你做了一套鸟舞服饰：一件在框架上编成的椰纤披肩，四排羽毛（{A}），一条绘有图案的 tapa 头带{B}，还和舞团一起在 tohua 上跳了 haka manu，8 次口令中有 {C} 次合拍。你的 manu 可以穿上它：上面的每一根羽毛都是在地上捡到的。","It flew off. Wait for the next one.":"它飞走了。等下一只吧。","You counted the birds of a valley of Ua Huka with the bird society: {A}% of the birds that came by, each named through the binoculars. About 1,800 pihiti live on the island today, the last of their kind, and the patiʻotiʻo is found nowhere else. Counting them again and again is how we know they are safe.":"你和鸟类协会一起数了 Ua Huka 一条山谷里的鸟：数到了飞过的鸟中的 {A}%，每一只都是通过望远镜认出名字的。如今岛上生活着约 1,800 只 pihiti，是这个物种最后的一群；patiʻotiʻo 也是别处都没有的。一次又一次地数它们，我们才知道它们是安全的。","Look again: that one is {A}.":"再看看：那一只是{A}。","Time. Your count: <b>{A} pihiti, {B} patiʻotiʻo, {C} upe</b>. There were {D}, {E} and {F}: you counted <b>{G}%</b> of the birds{H}.":"时间到。你的计数：<b>{A} 只 pihiti、{B} 只 patiʻotiʻo、{C} 只 upe</b>。实际有 {D}、{E} 和 {F} 只：你数到了 <b>{G}%</b> 的鸟{H}。","Tip checked {A} on the quay of Vaipaeʻe and found the rat hidden in {B}. The load was sealed, the rat caught in a trap before morning, and the five tracking tunnels showed only a crab and a gecko. On Ua Huka this check is done at every cargo ship, with dogs trained in New Zealand, and the tunnels are read every month.":"Tip 在 Vaipaeʻe 的码头上检查了{A}，发现老鼠藏在{B}里。货物被封好，老鼠在天亮前就落进了捕鼠器，五条足迹隧道里只留下一只螃蟹和一只壁虎的脚印。在 Ua Huka，每艘货轮到港都要做这样的检查，用的是在新西兰训练的狗，足迹隧道每个月都会查看。","Tie a {A}":"系上{A}","Trap {A}: empty.":"第 {A} 个捕鼠器：空的。","Tip sniffs {A} all round, wags and moves on: nothing there.":"Tip 把{A}四周嗅了一遍，摇摇尾巴走开了：那里什么也没有。",", with one wrong name on the way":"，途中叫错了一个名字",", with {A} wrong names on the way":"，途中叫错了 {A} 个名字","The emblem of the meʻae, on the rear platform. Carved in red volcanic tuff, <i>keetu</i>, it stands {#1} m above the ground: the largest tiki in French Polynesia. Look at its massive square head, and its left arm, partly broken.":"它是这座 meʻae 的象征，立在后方的平台上。用红色火山凝灰岩 <i>keetu</i> 雕成，高出地面 {#1} 米，是法属波利尼西亚最大的提基像。看看它巨大方正的头部，还有部分断裂的左臂。","UA HUKA":"UA HUKA","small and blue, in the flowers":"小小的、蓝色的，在花丛里","small and black, in the leaves":"小小的、黑色的，在树叶里","big and grey-blue, heavy on the branch":"大个子、灰蓝色，沉沉地压在树枝上",", with {#1} wrong names on the way":"，途中叫错了 {#1} 个名字"});
